  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental figures from the Totals column of the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (pp4-5): 1,133,539 + 2,016,819 - 2,106,854 + 27,330 - 28,330 + 135,000 = 1,177,504. Business-type from the Proprietary Funds Total column (pp6-7), measure = net position: 1,788,385 + 755,282 - 359,359 + 1,000 = 2,185,308; no single printed receipts/disbursements total so totals computed. Business-type Grant 181,553 not described as federal or state, so intergovernmental with review. Taxes 542,638 split using p2 (property 238,580+46,108, sales 229,270, motor vehicle 28,680) and p11/p13 (property 221,857 + 46,108 + 16,723 = 284,688). Attempt 3 (audit fix): Intergovernmental 600,018 split (split_from) using its components on pp11, 13, 15 and the Ambulance Board column on p4 (General 320,384 + Street 183,954 + Ambulance 75,000 + Other 20,680): state aid 412,206, Homestead Exemption 24,324, Property Tax Credit 23,274, Motor Vehicle Pro-Rate 621, In Lieu of Tax 28,247, motor vehicle tax 10,709, charges for services (NPPD lease) 93,207, franchise 7,430. Ambulance Board fund has no own schedule; its per-fund detail lines are not added (user: leave those). Miscellaneous 641,319 split using the column breakdowns (General Fund 446,084 on p11, Other 41,000 on p15): donations 307,456, licenses and permits 4,242, keno/lottery 3,731, other 325,890 (includes Ambulance Board 153,800, not itemized). Budget-and-actual all-funds statement (p10, budgetary basis, includes enterprise funds) not recorded in detail to avoid double counting with the basic statements. Detail: General Fund combining schedule recorded per column (5 sub-funds; sub-fund transfers net to -11,670 as in the governmental statement), Street Fund, Nonmajor funds per fund (3). Operating expenses mapped to professional/contract services (cash flow statement calls it contractual services). Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis, Total column (p1). Business-type detail: 'Water and Sewer' (= Combined Utility operating expenses 216,367, p7) and 'Sanitation' (= Sanitation fund 88,966, p7) disbursement lines from the all-funds budget schedule (p10); its receipts, capital outlay, debt service and totals mix governmental and business-type funds, so those are not added and no detail_totals entry is made (the earlier p10 note still holds for the governmental lines; the business-type funds have no other detail schedule). v7 re-trim added p9 (proprietary cash flow statement: reconciliation of operating income, net cash from operating activities 272,148); no new data; later page citations shifted +1. Read pages 1-15 of 15."
